Your only task is to produce five valid compact rating-vector strings.

Return a single compact JSON object with exactly these properties: "0", "1", "2", "3", "4".
Each property value must be one JSON string containing exactly 27 score:confidence pairs.
Scores are integers from 0 through 100. Confidences are from 0 through 1.
Separate the pairs with semicolons and use no spaces inside a vector string.
The final pair is Overall.
Do not return starId, ratings, index, statementId, arrays, nested objects, commentary, or markdown.
Do not use category positions 0 through 26 as scores.
Keep the JSON compact and preferably on one line.
